  "A guillotine table scores a straight line across a rectangle and breaks it. You cannot start a cut in the middle of the glass. So a valid arrangement has to be reachable by a sequence of edge-to-edge splits: cut the sheet in half, cut each half again, and so on. This is the constraint that makes nesting hard, and it is why an arrangement that looks efficient on screen can be uncuttable in reality.",
