  "A sheet has a purchase price per square metre and a selling price per square metre, and they answer different questions. Balance at cost tells you what is tied up on the racks. Balance at sell tells you what is available to earn. Both belong on the stock screen.",
  "A sheet store is only half the picture; the other half is what comes off the sheets. Below is the seeded job's own glass, nested on the seeded stock — {v1} panes of {v2} mm {v3} from {v4}, cut with the application's house profile for that thickness: a {v5} mm trim on all four edges and a {v6} mm blade gap.",
  "A shop does not quote glass by area alone. A pane too small to fill a square metre still costs a square metre of work, and one big enough to need a crane costs more per square metre than the rest of the specification. Both are in the pricing engine, both price every line on this page, and this job sits between them: its smallest lite is 0.80 m² and its largest is 3.84 m², so neither rule fires on it. Here they are on the panels that do.",
