  "An ERP that quietly recalculates yesterday's quote with today's glass prices is not an ERP. When sheet-store prices move, the affected row is flagged rather than silently rescored.",
  "An ERP that recalculates yesterday's quotation at today's glass prices is not an ERP. What ProGlass stores instead, and why it matters more than any feature.",
  "An estimator who could not find software that knew what an SGU air space was, and wrote one instead. The order below is the order it happened in — the last entry is the part still being decided.",
  "An estimator's background instead.",
  "An experienced WPF/.NET developer who can take a module end to end — view, view-model, service, tests — without being walked through the pattern each time.",
  "An expired licence degrades to read-only rather than locking you out of your data.",
  "An honest answer",
  "An inquiry becomes a quotation becomes a job order becomes a delivery becomes an invoice. Each step copies the previous record and keeps the audit trail, so the third version of a number never appears out of nowhere.",
  "An inquiry carries the customer, the project, a scope of supply and the attachments that came with the request. It is the record that survives the phone call, so the quotation that follows can be checked against what was asked.",
  "An investor or backer",
  "An invoice can enrich the company master but a missed field can never erase it.",
  "An operator or shop owner",
  "An operator ticked a job, the specification panel filled in, the pane checklist filled in — and the cutting-size list stayed empty. A first pass was made and a syntax fault corrected. The symptom survived it. So the next pass began by refusing to trust that first fix: it is described in the document as unverified and not defended, and nothing downstream was allowed to assume it had been right.",
  "An opt-in background pass that publishes finished proformas to this website's Records, Job Order and Deliveries pages. ProGlass stays the source of truth, the local workflows keep working offline, and no credential is ever written into the queue.",
