  "Generic ERP software assumes widgets: identical units, a bill of materials, a production order. Glass is not that. It is sold by area, priced on a build-up, cut from sheets, delivered in part-loads and invoiced against whatever actually left the yard. ProGlass Automation exists because that mismatch is where the money quietly goes missing.",
