  "Glass is bought on sheets and priced by area, and those buy prices change. When they do, every stored quotation that recalculates itself silently becomes a different quotation. If your profitability reporting reads those figures, your historical margin data is rewritten every time a supplier changes a rate.",
  "Glass is quoted by area, not by piece. The industry unit is the square metre (SQM), and pieces are described in millimetres: W for width, H for height. A unit with two different panes needs both, which is why quotations often show W1 / H1 / W2 / H2 — the outer pane and the inner pane measured separately. Linear metres (LM) appear where an edge treatment is priced by the length of edge rather than by area.",
