  "I am a developer, not a funder. What is the most useful thing I can do?",
  "I came to this from the glass trade, not from software. I am not a company, I do not have a team, and I have written this in the hours around a job that also expects me to estimate. What I do have is a product that works, a record of everything that is wrong with it, and no intention of letting it stop here.",
  "IBM Plex Sans",
  "If a licence expires past its grace period, the application degrades to read-only rather than locking you away from your records — you can still open and export your data. Renewal is a new licence file dropped in the same place; the application records both events in its audit log.",
  "If an answer here is thinner than you would like, that is usually because the honest answer is still being worked out — not because it is being avoided.",
  "If it keeps happening, the reference above is what the developer needs — send it to",
  "If optimization is part of your day, bring a real cutting list.",
  "If that describes your business, see it working.",
  "If the application does not do something, this page says so rather than leaving it ambiguous.",
  "If the profit figure changes depending on when you opened the screen, it cannot be used to price the next job. It has to be written once and read forever.",
  "If the software does something useful for you, tell one other fabricator. That is genuinely the most effective thing on this list.",
  "If the stock screen holds one quantity per item and someone edits it down from 40 to 38, the reason is gone. Nobody can say whether those two sheets were sold, broken, cut wrong or counted wrong — and the same edit can happen again next week.",
  "If this raised a question about how the software handles something specific, ask it directly — you are writing to the person who builds it.",
  "If you are a glass fabricator, a WPF developer, a translator or simply someone who thinks a one-person industrial product is worth backing, there is a slot below that fits what you already have.",
  "If you make glass, fund small industrial software, supply machines, translate, test, or simply run a shop that does the job this is for — there is a slot below written for you specifically, with what it asks for and what it returns.",
  "If you only read part of this page, these are the ones that decide whether the software fits: estimation, optimization, stock, dispatch, margin and reporting.",
