  "Snapshot-based",
  "So an estimator does the last step by hand: another window, another PDF, a figure typed into a quote, and nothing that checks it afterwards.",
  "Sole author",
  "Sole developer of ProGlass Automation: estimation, optimization, production and finance workflows for glass fabrication.",
  "Some optimizers place rectangles anywhere on the sheet. A glass table cannot work that way — it scores a line, breaks the sheet, and the piece comes free. So the engine models the cuts, not just the positions: it splits the remaining rectangle at each placement and records the split as a cut in the order the operator will make it.",
  "Someone at a manufacturer or a large processor who owns the performance data for their own products.",
  "Someone who enjoys breaking software on purpose: property-based tests for the nesting engine, fault injection around the document chain, and regression cases written from real customer scenarios.",
  "Someone who needs a defensible quotation out the same day, built from costs the business actually buys at.",
  "Someone who runs the day this software is for, willing to say where it is wrong.",
  "Someone who would rather fund a specific industrial product than a general pitch.",
  "Someone who writes procedures for real operators: task-based guides for the eight production stages, the proforma wizard and the sheet store, written from the screen rather than from the code.",
  "Someone who writes WPF and wants to work on a real product with real users.",
