  "Then the terms, in writing",
  "There are 2,369 xUnit test methods across 288 files, and the workflow invariants — piece flow clamping, VAT tolerance, price-basis stamping — are the ones that must never regress.",
  "There are three ways to activate, all of which end with the licence file in the right place:",
  "There is a failure mode in quotation software that is worse than a crash, because it does not look like a failure. The software is asked for last month's job. It reopens the quotation, re-reads the current sheet prices, and recomputes. The margin on screen is now a number that nobody ever quoted.",
  "There is more software here than there are hours to finish it.",
  "There is no application form and no portal. The reply comes from the person who writes the code, and it will be honest about whether the fit is right — including when it is not.",
  "There is no cloud account, no tenant and no subscription dashboard. The application runs on one Windows PC, or on a handful that share a database file across the office.",
  "There is no CV here, because a CV is the part of a person you cannot check. What exists instead is six working documents at the root of the repository, each carrying the date it was written, describing what broke, what the evidence was, what changed and what is still open. Read together they are a working history of the software — and of its author — more specific than any biography.",
  "There is no mobile application and no mobile interface.",
  "There is no office, no second developer, no designer, no translator and no one on support. The build is as far along as one estimator working evenings could take it. The next stage needs help, and the gaps are listed by name rather than hinted at.",
  "There is no price on this page, and that is deliberate.",
  "There is no sales team and no support queue between you and the developer. Mention “sponsorship” or the specific gap you are interested in, and the reply will come from {v1}.",
  "There is no sponsorship platform wired up yet, no tier list and no published amounts. Until there is, this is a conversation by email — which suits a product built this way.",
  "There is no subscription, no telemetry and no funding behind the project. Certificates, signing, the test hardware and the time spent on a release all come out of one person's pocket.",
  "There is no support tier between a customer and the author. Describe the job you do and where it goes wrong, and the answer comes back from the person who can change the software — usually with a question about how your shop actually works.",
  "Thermal",
  "Thermal toughening furnace: bed layout composition, heating zone profile, quench pressure, cycle time and fragmentation test logging.",
  "These are not aspirations written on a wall. Each is enforced somewhere in the build, which is why they have survived at this size — and why a solo author can still answer for the result.",
  "These are the application's four families. Pressing one re-themes this page, which is exactly what it does to the application.",
  "These are the defaults the engineering assumes before an operator changes anything. Every value is editable per run, and 'Load house defaults' puts them back.",
  "These are the stages the application reports its search through. The plan itself is computed the moment the run starts, so what you are watching is the sequence, not a long calculation.",
  "These are the stages the application reports its search through. This preview computes the plan in the browser the moment it starts, so what you are watching is the sequence, not a long calculation.",
  "These modules are explicitly listed as ungated, so a missing entry can never be mistaken for a deliberate free one. A test fails the build if a new module ships without somebody deciding either way.",
  "These names are not partners.",
  "They are named because their published figures are what an estimator working on a Gulf specification reaches for, and the module is designed to hold data from any manufacturer. None of these companies has been contacted, none is involved in this project, and none has agreed to anything. If that changes, the agreement is what this page will say — and it will say it in writing, with the date.",
