  "Twenty-two lines, priced three ways.",
  "Two decimal places, half away from zero, and 5% VAT. The arithmetic on this page is performed the same way rather than copied from the file, and a build-time check fails if the two ever disagree.",
  "Two different things are covered here, and they behave very differently. This website is a set of static pages. The application is desktop software that keeps your business data on your own machine.",
  "Two independent dials: how wide the search is, and how hard it pushes.",
  "Two independent oracles check every optimization result, and a plan that fails either one is shown but never exported. The tests are invariants rather than getters — they assert what has to be true, which is what someone who does not trust himself writes.",
  "Two optimizers can produce very different-looking plans for the same cutting list, and both can be correct. The difference is what the table can physically do.",
  "Two oracles run over every result and check different things. A plan that fails either one is still displayed so it can be inspected — but it is never exported to a cut file and never fed to production work.",
  "Two panels at the edges of the two rules: a 400 × 300 mm vent light billed at the 0.5 m² floor, and a 2400 × 1800 mm atrium lite priced at base plus 20% because it reaches 4 m².",
  "Two panes bonded across a PVB interlayer",
  "Two panes re-cut after breakage.",
  "Two rules, and neither is a rounding.",
  "Two services, deliberately not one. The application log is a rolling terminal — TIME · LEVEL · MODULE / FUNCTION · entry, the last 500 kept in memory, counters for errors (critical included) and warnings, and a button that opens the folder of dated log files. It carries a correlation ID (CORR-XXXXXX) and a document ID, so one business operation can be followed from the inquiry all the way to the statement even though the work happened in different modules and on different days. The audit trail is the other half: business events rather than diagnostics, written as who changed which record, with the before and after of every field, and grouped into the canonical sections held as constants so a typo can never split one section into two.",
  "Two services, deliberately not one. The application log records what happened — startup, licence, seeding, production, errors — and the audit trail records the business events, with the before and after of every field. The correlation ID on a traceable entry follows one operation from the inquiry to the statement, across modules and across days.",
